fix(monkeymux): scope the capability hint to the attached client

Review follow-ups on the capability hint.

The hint describes the terminal that is actually attached, so caching one
session-wide let a client that declares none — an older helper, or a plain
terminal running `monkeymux attach` — have a previous client's identity
advertised to its background windows. Store the hint on the attach client
and resolve it from the primary client, falling back to the session hint
only while no client is registered, which is the upgrade-restore window
this mechanism exists for.

The per-window answer budget also only reset when a visible window
produced output, so a window shown without printing anything kept an
exhausted budget and could not be answered the next time it ran in the
background. Reset it wherever a terminal starts showing the window.

Adds regression coverage for the client-scoped hint, the budget reset
across a visibility cycle, and a probe split across pty reads still
fencing the DA1 that follows it. Renames the mid-chunk fence test to
describe what it actually asserts.

